
Usage:  LNCOP  objfile [,objfile ...]] [@cmdfile]  [options]

Option

/[NO]Briefmap              - specify full or brief map format
/[NO]Crossref              - enable/disable cross reference table listing
/[NO]Debug                 - enable/disable debugger symbols to COFF file
/[NO]ECho                  - enable/disable echoing of command files
/EXtract=(libs=modules)    - extract module(s) from library(s)
/EXTRACTSymbol=(libs=syms) - extract symbol(s) from library(s)
/FIle=bankfile             - read command from file (default extension = .fil)
/Format=type[=args]        - specify output object module format.  this
                             may be coff, hex, lm. Optional arguments
                             may be specified for some types.
/Ignoreerrors              - force object module even if errors
/LIBDirectory=directory    - specify directory for library file search
/LIBFile=(libs[=syms])     - specify library file
/Load=objfile,..           - load object module(s). Primarily for /FILE file
/[NO]LOCalsymbols          - enable/disable assembly local symbols to crossref 



?+




/Mapfile[=file]            - specify load map file
/NOMapfile                 - disable load map file
/Outputfile[=file]         - specify output object file
/NOOutputfile              - inhibit object file
/Range=(ranges)            - specify memory range(s)
/Sect=section=address      - specify section address or range
/SIzesect=section=size     - specify section size
/[NO]Tablesymbols          - enable/disable symbol table listing
/[NO]Warnings              - enable/disable warning messages
/[NO]Xdirectory            - enable/disable searching standard directories for
                             include files


The above commands may also be used within a Link File (/FILE)
without the leading / and only one command per line; to load
object modules, use LOAD command.



?-
